## UI Todos

Make the UX feel seamless

- [x] Make UX for search better
  - [x] Add shift + click for range selection in checkbox lists
        (SecretsList, GlobalSearchModal) - Ctrl/Cmd+click needed no new
        code since every checkbox click was already additive/non-exclusive.
  - [x] Wrap each row's name in a `<label htmlFor>` associated with its
        checkbox so clicking the name also toggles selection.
- [ ] Have better onboarding and help UX
  - [ ] Custom onboarding flow to help users understand how to use the
        app - deferred, too open-ended to build without more direction
        on what it should actually contain/look like.
  - [x] Help menu button (header, next to Search) opens a modal covering
        FAQs and the "No profile selected" troubleshooting steps (export
        first, clear site data, reload).

## Bug todos

- [x] Vault-load-failure self-healing: `Index.tsx` now shows a "reloading
      in a few seconds" message and calls `window.location.reload()`
      after 3s when `dbState.status === "error"`.
  - Skipped the "after Clerk sign-in" half of this - the concrete symptom
    that most plausibly motivated it ("No profile selected") was already
    root-caused to a hydration race and fixed earlier via
    `collections.config.preload()`, and there's no other clear failure
    signal after a Clerk sign-in to hook a reload off of.

- [x] `DOCS/code/api-spend-and-auth.md`: fixed the contradictory paragraph
      (browser calls the same-origin `/api/proxy-spend`; the server-side
      proxy calls the provider's billing endpoint with the forwarded key).

- [x] `FolderSidebar.tsx` / `SecretRow.tsx` drag handles: removed the
      `role="button"`/`tabIndex={0}` that advertised keyboard operability
      the handles never actually had (`onKeyDown` only stopped
      propagation). Kept `aria-label` - the e2e drag-and-drop tests locate
      handles by it regardless of role. Full keyboard-driven reordering
      (grab/move/drop via arrow keys) is still unimplemented and was
      already out of scope per the original drag-and-drop plan.

- [x] `Index.tsx`: `PayWall`/`SpendTab` no longer `forceMount` - they now
      mount only once the API Spend tab is actually activated (Radix's
      default), and `GlobalSearchModal` is only rendered at all once
      `isSearchOpen` is true instead of always being mounted behind
      `Suspense`.
